menu "CEC persistence (NVS / persist-on-fault)"

    config CEC_PERSIST_WRITE_BUDGET_MS
        int "Persist-on-fault trigger-to-durable-commit budget (ms)"
        default 10
        help
            The persist-on-fault contract's binding end-to-end budget
            (firmware/contracts/persist-on-fault.md): on the power-fail
            interrupt the gasp must complete ISR entry, load shedding,
            the RAM-tail write, commit/index programming, and durable
            completion within this many milliseconds. It is never a bulk
            dump, and the persist region is pre-erased in normal operation.

            The default 10 sits under the current-BETA conservative
            sudden-loss paper bound of 11.96 ms at the reviewed 215.386 mA
            rail load (including 20% design margin), minimum 3760 uF,
            worst-case SS14 drop, and 85% conversion. This leaves 1.96 ms
            model margin. OQ-56 must still validate ESR, temperature,
            aging, slow brownout, source decay, and real durable-commit
            latency. Re-tests update this default and the contract together;
            firmware must never re-hardcode the number.

endmenu
